cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite the paper given under
  preferred-citation and the thesis listed under references.
type: software
title: "chapter3_pollinators: ORAA, P-MADDPG and LToS in the Pollinators' Game"
abstract: >-
  The experiments of Chapter 3 of the thesis: the Pollinators' Game, a
  property-based commons dilemma in land use; the P-MADDPG landowner learners;
  the ORAA regulatory agent (Online Regulatory Agent Algorithm) in its
  Model-based and Omniscient forms; the reward-shape baseline; LToS as a
  learned reward-sharing baseline; and the campaign and analysis code that
  produce the chapter's tables and figures.
